{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-cs-gram-determinant-ratio","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:cs-gram-determinant-ratio","kind":"definition","title":"Chern--Simons Gram-determinant ratio $\\kappa$","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-em-coupling-chern-simons"],"tags":["gram-matrix","chern-simons","kappa","determinant"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.Archimedean.csGramDetRatio","text":"cs-gram-determinant-ratio.md","leanSource":"cs-gram-determinant-ratio.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:cs-gram-determinant-ratio\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">G^{\\mathrm{cl}}_{\\mathrm{CS}}</code> and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">G^{q}_{\\mathrm{CS}}</code> be the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">2 \\times 2</code> Gram matrices of the classical and the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-deformed Chern--Simons pairing on the rank-<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">2</code> sublattice spanned by the force carriers <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T_{2,9}</code> and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T_{3,5}</code> on Bring's surface (<a href=\"#rem:em-coupling-chern-simons\" data-at=\"predicted-spectra/em-completeness-gauge-coupling\">Chern--Simons descent correction</a>), both written in one common basis, with <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\det G^{q}_{\\mathrm{CS}} \\neq 0</code>. The <strong>Gram-determinant ratio</strong> is</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\kappa \\;:=\\; \\frac{\\det G^{\\mathrm{cl}}_{\\mathrm{CS}}}{\\det G^{q}_{\\mathrm{CS}}}.</code></pre>\n<p>A change of basis <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">B</code> with <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\det B \\neq 0</code> sends each Gram matrix <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">G</code> to <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">B^{\\top} G B</code> and multiplies each determinant by <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(\\det B)^2</code>, so <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\kappa</code> does not depend on the basis chosen.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/cs-gram-determinant-ratio.md","heading":"Definition","number":"16.6.8","page":"b/def-cs-gram-determinant-ratio","lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.MassTheory.Archimedean.csGramDetRatio","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/cs-gram-determinant-ratio.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
